# Contributing to facebook-marketplace-scraper

Thanks for stopping by. This is a small portfolio project, so the rules are
short — but the credential rules are non-negotiable.

## Setup

```bash
python -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e ".[dev]"        # tests + lint
pip install -e ".[facebook]"   # only if you need the live Facebook path
python -m pytest tests/ -v
ruff check src tests && ruff format --check src tests
```

## No-credentials policy (read this first)

- NEVER commit `auth_state.json`, `.env` / `.env.*`, cookies, tokens, or
  session files. They are listed in `.gitignore` AND rejected by CI (the
  secret-scan job fails the build if they are tracked, and gitleaks scans
  the full history).
- The Facebook manual login (`auth_state.json`) uses a dedicated test
  account you own, on a stable IP, and the file stays on your machine.
- If you accidentally stage a credential file, stop and tell a maintainer
  before pushing — history rewrites are handled case by case.

## Fixture-first development

- CI never touches live Facebook: `FB_FIXTURE=1` is set in the test job and
  the Facebook adapter falls back to `tests/fixtures/fb_listings.json`
  whenever no `auth_state.json` exists.
- New Facebook behavior MUST ship with fixture coverage. To record a new
  fixture case, run locally against your own session, sanitize it (no
  personal data, no tokens), and add it under `tests/fixtures/`.
- Any test requiring live network access to Facebook must be marked to skip
  in CI. MercadoLibre tests use mocked HTTP (`httpx` mock transports).

## Scraping etiquette for contributors

- Keep result limits gentle (the `MAX_LIMIT = 60` clamp exists for a
  reason). Do not add proxy rotation, checkpoint bypasses, 2FA automation,
  or concurrency escalation — PRs in that direction will be closed.
- Respect `DISCLAIMER` (educational use, ToS compliance) in every change.

## PR checklist

- [ ] `pytest tests/` green (or `xvfb-run -a pytest`, as CI runs it)
- [ ] `ruff check src tests` and `ruff format --check src tests` clean
- [ ] No credentials, state files, or personal data in the diff
- [ ] README updated if flags, env vars, or behavior changed
- [ ] Fixture coverage for any new adapter parsing logic
